Z||000005||LZeitgeist||09-23-2001||12:03 PM||||Just my two cents ('cuz, well, you *asked* for 'em...)<P>Dump it. If you're going to put a wing on it, make it a Fiero wing... anything else looks like you're trying make it something it's not, and that unavoidably reflects back onto whoever's driving it. <P>My *only* exception to that opinion is the wing off a mid-80's Fierbird or Trans Am (the 'Knight Rider/K.I.T.T. body style). They fit perfectly (I always thought they'd hang over on the ends, but shockingly enough, the Fiero is the exact same width at the back as a Firebird), aren't as chunky-looking as the OEM Fiero wing, but still have a really nice clean look to them. If you're dead set against the OEM Fiero wing, try one of those - you may be pleasantly surprised.<P><BR>(Oh, and if it were me, I'd lose the wheel spinners, too... but that's just me.)<P><BR>-----------------   <P>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>White 1988 Coupe - (Dad's - the "Indy Fiero II")<BR>Red 1988 Formula - (ain't changin' a damn thing...)<BR>1st Place - Stock Coupe class -FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>3rd Place - Stock Formula class - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>Class Winner - 1982 to Present - Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show 2001<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
